# Walkthrough - Sliding Panel Auth Redesign

I have implemented a professional "Sliding Panel" authentication layout, inspired by your reference. This design features a tactile, high-end experience where the content shifts horizontally to reveal the appropriate form.

## Key Features

### 1. Sliding Overlay Panel
- A fixed-size glassmorphism card now houses both forms.
- A vibrant blue overlay panel (Side A) slides horizontally over the forms.
- The panel uses a custom ease function `[0.6, 0.05, -0.01, 0.9]` to feel "mechanical" and weighted.

### 2. Strategic Form Placement
- **LoginForm**: Fixed on the right half of the main card.
- **RegisterForm**: Fixed on the left half of the main card.
- As the overlay slides, it reveals the form underneath, creating a sophisticated "sliding drawer" effect.

### 3. Integrated DevTips
- The [DevTips](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/DevTips.tsx#25-81) now reside permanently inside the sliding overlay.
- Typography has been scaled down to fit perfectly within the 50% width of the overlay without feeling cramped.

### 4. Cohesive Design Line
- Maintained the DevAuth dark theme colors, shimmering gradients, and glowing background blobs.
- Subtle background decor (floating circles/rectangles) added inside the sliding panel for extra depth.

